WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.520
"The Santa Clause" came out back in 1994, so&nbsp;
while no one from the cast actually became Santa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.240
they have definitely aged. Keep watching for&nbsp;
how the cast of this holiday classic looks now.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.720
At the time The Santa Clause was released,&nbsp;
Tim Allen was already an established star in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.560
the realms of stand-up comedy and sitcoms,&nbsp;
thanks to his hit series Home Improvement.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.000
Playing Scott Calvin quickly made him a&nbsp;
film star, something that was cemented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.040
just a year later by his voice role as Buzz&nbsp;
Lightyear in Pixar's debut feature, Toy Story.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.840
“To infinity and beyond!”

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.320
The Santa Clause kicked off a string&nbsp;
of comedy films for Allen throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.920
the 1990s and early 2000s, including Jungle 2&nbsp;
Jungle, For Richer or Poorer, and Galaxy Quest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:45.120
After Home Improvement ended in 1999 he continued&nbsp;
acting in films — including the two Santa Clause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:51.360
sequels in 2002 and 2006 — until his return to&nbsp;
sitcom stardom in 2011 with Last Man Standing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.920
Allen continues to play his signature role of the&nbsp;
lovably in-over-his-head dad as he nears three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:01.040
decades of acting work, and after six seasons&nbsp;
on ABC, Last Man Standing has a new home at FOX&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.320
as of the fall of 2018. He also went on to voice&nbsp;
Buzz Lightyear in all four of the Toy Story films.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.960
Charlie Calvin is an eager young man whose&nbsp;
only wish is to get right to work helping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.240
his father be the best Santa he can&nbsp;
be. This includes even going as far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.840
as journeying to the North Pole to help&nbsp;
the elves design and build a new sleigh.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.920
Eric Lloyd, who played Charlie, shared a&nbsp;
similar work ethic throughout the 1990s.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.200
Though he's best known for his role in&nbsp;
The Santa Clause and its two sequels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.440
Lloyd has plenty of other acting credits to&nbsp;
his name dating back to age two. Back then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.520
he appeared as young Kevin on The Wonder Years.&nbsp;
After The Santa Clause came along and made him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:37.680
even more visible, he continued to work steadily&nbsp;
for the rest of the decade, playing a young Bruce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.800
Wayne in Batman &amp; Robin, and landing a recurring&nbsp;
role on the Christina Applegate-led sitcom Jesse.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.720
These days, Lloyd spends much of his time&nbsp;
behind the camera. After graduating from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.880
Chapman University with a degree in film&nbsp;
production, he co-founded LP Studios,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.080
a production and post-production company&nbsp;
for the film and music industries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.200
His work includes everything from&nbsp;
sound mixing to cinematography.

00:01:58.963 --> 00:02:02.400
David Krumholtz's screen acting career was just&nbsp;
beginning when he landed the role of Bernard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.720
He’s the grumpy but ultimately compassionate head&nbsp;
elf who guides Scott and Charlie through their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.880
North Pole journey and ultimately provides a way&nbsp;
for the father and son to stay in contact at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:16.320
end of the film. Krumholtz's acting career gained&nbsp;
considerable steam throughout the 1990s and 2000s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.520
so much so that while he reprised&nbsp;
his role for The Santa Clause 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:23.920
he was unable to return for The Santa Clause 3:&nbsp;
The Escape Clause because of another commitment.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:26.000
“Where’d he go?”

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.920
That commitment was Krumholtz's other best-known&nbsp;
role: mathematician Charlie Eppes on the hit CBS&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:39.760
drama Numb3rs, a role he played for five years&nbsp;
and nearly 120 episodes. To this day Krumholtz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.680
continues to work regularly in both film and&nbsp;
television, more recently appearing in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.160
TV series Living Biblically and The Deuce,&nbsp;
and films like The Ballad of Buster Scruggs.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.160
An acclaimed talent in the United&nbsp;
States as well as her native Canada,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.320
Wendy Crewson worked regularly throughout&nbsp;
the 1980s in film and television. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.240
she landed the role of Laura Miller in The&nbsp;
Santa Clause. Like her frequent scene partner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.560
Judge Reinhold, she grew from non-believer&nbsp;
to supporter and ally in Scott Calvin's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.040
Santa adventures. And the film's popularity&nbsp;
allowed her to return for both of its sequels.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.000
Crewson also continued to work&nbsp;
regularly after The Santa Clause,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.920
and gained higher-profile roles in American&nbsp;
film and television because of it. Among her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.520
other major credits after the film are&nbsp;
Air Force One, starring Harrison Ford,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.760
and the Canadian supernatural medical drama&nbsp;
Saving Hope, in which she co-starred for five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:29.760
seasons between 2012 and 2017. In 2016, the&nbsp;
Canadian Screen Awards presented her with its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.080
Earle Grey Award, recognizing her lifetime&nbsp;
of contributions to television in Canada.

00:03:35.585 --> 00:03:38.880
Judge Reinhold was already an established name&nbsp;
as an actor by the time The Santa Clause was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.960
made. But unlike Tim Allen — who was on the&nbsp;
rise — Reinhold had already faced a decade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:46.320
of ups and downs in the film industry.&nbsp;
After hits like Beverly Hills Cop and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:50.320
Fast Times at Ridgemont High, he'd also&nbsp;
dealt with major flops like Vice Versa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:54.720
and had retreated back into supporting roles. The&nbsp;
Santa Clause introduced him to a new audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.800
and as Dr. Neil Miller he was beloved and&nbsp;
brought back for both of the film's sequels.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.800
Since The Santa Clause Reinhold has also&nbsp;
continued to work steadily in film and television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.840
including appearing in the series Arrested&nbsp;
Development and the 2017 film Bad Grandmas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.000
as well as many other guest star appearances.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.120
Like Allen, Lloyd, Crewson, and Reinhold, Peter&nbsp;
Boyle also has the distinction of appearing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:19.440
all three films in the Santa Clause trilogy,&nbsp;
but unlike them, he played different roles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.760
Boyle — whose film acting career was already&nbsp;
well-established and nearly three decades old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.600
at the time of the original film — played&nbsp;
Scott's boss Mr. Whittle in the first film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.920
He was then brought back to play Father Time in&nbsp;
both The Santa Clause 2 and The Santa Clause 3.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.880
Boyle's career before The Santa&nbsp;
Clause was already well-established,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.960
and included celebrated roles in everything&nbsp;
from Young Frankenstein to Taxi Driver,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:42.640
but it was what happened after the first film&nbsp;
was released that made him a household name.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:47.360
Boyle was cast as Frank Barone on the massively&nbsp;
successful sitcom Everybody Loves Raymond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.760
for which he received seven consecutive Emmy Award&nbsp;
nominations for Outstanding Supporting Actor in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:57.840
a Comedy Series. Unfortunately, Boyle passed&nbsp;
away on December 12, 2006, at the age of 71.

